kind":"text"},{"text":"wheelRadius","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VehicleWheel3D\/wheelRadius","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/vehiclewheel3d\/wheelradius","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The radius of the wheel in meters.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/VehicleWheel3D/useAsTraction":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VehicleWheel3D\/useAsTraction","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":", this wheel transfers engine force to the ground to propel the vehicle forward. This value is used in conjunction with "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VehicleBody3D\/engineForce"},{"type":"text","text":" and ignored if you are using the per-wheel "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VehicleWheel3D\/engineForce"},{"type":"text","text":" value instead."}],"title":"useAsTraction","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/vehiclewheel3d\/useastraction","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"useAsTraction"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/VehicleWheel3D/brake":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/vehiclewheel3d\/brake","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VehicleWheel3D\/brake","abstract":[{"text":"Slows down the wheel by applying a braking force. The wheel is only slowed down if it is in contact with a surface. The force you need to apply to adequately slow down your vehicle depends on the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/RigidBody3D\/mass","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" of the vehicle. For a vehicle with a mass set to 1000, try a value in the 25 - 30 range for hard braking.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"brake"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"brake"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/VehicleBody3D":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/vehiclebody3d","title":"VehicleBody3D","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A 3D physics body that simulates the behavior of a car."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VehicleBody3D","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"VehicleBody3D","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"VehicleBody3D","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/VehicleWheel3D/suspensionMaxForce":{"type":"topic","title":"suspensionMaxForce","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/vehiclewheel3d\/suspensionmaxforce","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VehicleWheel3D\/suspensionMaxForce","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The maximum force the spring can resist. This value should be higher than a quarter of the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/RigidBody3D\/mass","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" of the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VehicleBody3D","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" or the spring will not carry the weight of the vehicle. Good results are often obtained by a value that is about 3× to 4× this number."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"suspensionMaxForce"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double"}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/VehicleWheel3D/getSkidinfo()":{"type":"topic","title":"getSkidinfo()","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/vehiclewheel3d\/getskidinfo()","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VehicleWheel3D\/getSkidinfo()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"getSkidinfo"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Returns a value between 0.0 and 1.0 that indicates whether this wheel is skidding. 0.0 is skidding (the wheel has lost grip, e.g. icy terrain), 1.0 means not skidding (the wheel has full grip, e.g. dry asphalt road).","type":"text"}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/VehicleBody3D/steering":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"steering"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/vehiclebody3d\/steering","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The steering angle for the vehicle. Setting this to a non-zero value will result in the vehicle turning when it’s moving. Wheels that have ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VehicleWheel3D\/useAsSteering","isActive":true},{"text":" set to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"text":" will automatically be rotated.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VehicleBody3D\/steering","kind":"symbol","title":"steering"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/VehicleWheel3D/wheelFrictionSlip":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"This determines how much grip this wheel has. It is combined with the friction setting of the surface the wheel is in contact with. 0.0 means no grip, 1.0 is normal grip. For a drift car setup, try setting the grip of the rear wheels slightly lower than the front wheels, or use a lower value to simulate tire wear."}],"role":"symbol","title":"wheelFrictionSlip","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"wheelFrictionSlip"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VehicleWheel3D\/wheelFrictionSlip","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/vehiclewheel3d\/wheelfrictionslip"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/VehicleWheel3D/wheelRestLength":{"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"wheelRestLength","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"title":"wheelRestLength","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VehicleWheel3D\/wheelRestLength","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"This is the distance in meters the wheel is lowered from its origin point. Don’t set this to 0.0 and move the wheel into position, instead move the origin point of your wheel (the gizmo in Godot) to the position the wheel will take when bottoming out, then use the rest length to move the wheel down to the position it should be in when the car is in rest."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/vehiclewheel3d\/wheelrestlength","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"}}}